{"id": "EUVD-2026-59335", "enisaUuid": "1ffd3bf5-e277-3037-9a0f-85b80f4ef8ea", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: ipset: Don't use test_bit() in lockless RCU readers in hash types\n\nSashiko pointed out that there are a few lockless RCU readers\nusing test_bit() which is a relaxed atomic operation and\nprovides no memory barrier guarantees. Use test_bit_acquire()\ninstead where the operation may run parallel with add/del/gc,\ni.e. is not one from the next cases\n\n- protected by region lock\n- in a set destroy phase\n- in a new/temporary set creation phase", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:24", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c107233d2ff4fd7cef5d02f9124b99194957a710", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6329d3a9afe715fddda0460cfa46b496d61c2fe0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7445fe965b7d8756070a40e80f8b73348ccda1d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c4d257734e91bfcdc71d41843392dd6400b5bb1b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3219d74e4536658c937fd878a327257b86ce80dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e4b4984e28c16406ecb318444dea4a8bf47def3e"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72436", "GHSA-6x4x-6p4p-6f5f"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.71, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02c5aa64-e379-36a5-82e0-567ef0ae5dab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "18f84d41d34fa35d0d64bbaea01fe664553ecc06 <e4b4984e28c16406ecb318444dea4a8bf47def3e"}, {"id": "0f1b6911-eb94-3218-867e-9216dcb8bf05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "18f84d41d34fa35d0d64bbaea01fe664553ecc06 <3219d74e4536658c937fd878a327257b86ce80dd"}, {"id": "14b9ec40-a017-3308-9dff-9a75812c4c4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "18f84d41d34fa35d0d64bbaea01fe664553ecc06 <c107233d2f